h1. Silver Validated Layer: Data Quality and Quarantine


h2. Purpose


The Silver validated layer is the quality boundary between Bronze source data and downstream Silver transformations. It has two responsibilities:

# Validate schema and data quality for each Bronze record.
# Publish passing records to {{silver_validated}} and preserve failed records in centralized quarantine.

||Scope||Implementation||
|Source tables|41 tables across Card, Customer, Transaction, and Financial Crime|
|Static data-quality rules|76 rules covering 34 tables|
|Additional controls|Schema rescue, duplicate national identity, duplicate active business key, and post-validation checks|
|Valid output|{{silver_validated.<table_name>}}|
|Failed output|{{governance.silver_quarantine_record}}|


h2. 1. Validate schema and data quality


h3. Validation tasks


||Pipeline task||Responsibility||
|{{validate_and_route}}|Reads Bronze changes, validates schema and data quality once, and routes each record to validated Silver or quarantine.|
|{{silver_validation_audit}}|Confirms business-key uniqueness, valid SCD2 intervals, and that published validated rows still pass their configured rules. It also assigns the job run ID to new quarantine records.|


h3. Validation sequence


||Step||Implementation||
|1|Read Bronze Change Data Feed records of type {{insert}} and {{update_postimage}}.|
|2|Capture the complete incoming Bronze record as JSON evidence before normalization or validation.|
|3|Normalize configured identifiers, email, and phone values.|
|4|Evaluate the table's static rules and any applicable duplicate controls. A rule result of {{FALSE}} or SQL {{NULL}} is a failure.|
|5|Treat non-empty {{_rescued_data}} as a schema failure named {{RESCUED_DATA_PRESENT}}.|
|6|Set {{is_quarantined}} when at least one rule or schema check fails.|


h3. Data-quality rules and their implementation


||Rule type||Examples||Implementation||Failure handling||
|Required-field completeness|Missing identifiers, references, amounts, dates, timestamps, or statuses|Evaluate explicit {{column IS NOT NULL}} predicates after normalization.|Add the stable rule name to the failure list.|
|Reference resolution|{{account_id = -1}}, {{UNKNOWN-CARD}}, {{UNKNOWN-CUSTOMER}}|Evaluate table-specific predicates that reject documented unresolved reference values.|Quarantine the complete source record.|
|Format and permitted values|Invalid PAN, malformed email, placeholder phone, unknown response/risk/reason code, invalid currency|Evaluate comparisons, allowed-value checks, and minimum-length checks.|Quarantine under the matching format or domain rule.|
|Numeric and business ranges|Negative income or balance, alert score outside 0–100, negative credit amount|Evaluate numeric ranges and conditional business predicates.|Quarantine under the matching range rule.|
|Temporal validity|Card status timestamp before 2020 or in the future|Evaluate an inclusive timestamp range using the current processing timestamp.|Quarantine under the timestamp range rule.|
|Duplicate national identity|Duplicate active {{national_id}} in Core Banking or CRM|Normalize active records, group by {{national_id}}, and join duplicate values into validation.|Add {{<table>__national_id__duplicate}}.|
|Duplicate active business key|More than one current row for an SCD2 business key|Group current Bronze rows by the configured business key and identify counts greater than one.|Add {{<table>__<business_key>__duplicate_active}}.|
|Schema rescue|Non-empty {{_rescued_data}} on any source table|Check rescued schema content independently of static rules.|Add {{RESCUED_DATA_PRESENT}} and preserve the rescued content.|


Static rule coverage is distributed as follows:

||Domain||Source tables||Tables with static rules||Static rules||
|Card|5|5|36|
|Customer|7|7|14|
|Transaction|10|8|11|
|Financial Crime|19|14|15|
|*Total*|*41*|*34*|*76*|


Seven tables do not have a static row predicate: {{transaction_channel}}, {{merchant}}, {{investigation_case_card_fraud_flag}}, {{investigation_case}}, {{investigation_note}}, {{watchlist}}, and {{call_center_log}}. They still pass through normalization, schema-rescue validation, active-key checking, routing, and the Silver validation audit.

Reconciliation, late-arrival handling, immutable-event replay deduplication, and reference-data monitoring are not single-row quarantine rules. Those controls are handled in the appropriate ingestion, event-processing, or downstream reconciliation stage.

h3. Complete static rule implementation


Every predicate below is evaluated against the normalized record. When a predicate is false or null, its stable rule name is added to the record's failure list.

