h2. 2. Quarantine failed records


!scd2-cdc-workflow.png|alt=SCD2 and CDC processing workflow!


The same assessment result controls both outputs. Passing records are published to their source-aligned validated Silver table. Failed records are excluded from that validated output and written to centralized quarantine.

Quarantine handling follows four principles:

||Principle||Implementation||
|Preserve evidence|Capture the complete Bronze record before normalization and keep it in {{quarantine_data_payload}}.|
|Keep failures atomic|A record failing two rules produces two quarantine rows, one for each {{failed_rule_name}}.|
|Avoid stale SCD2 failures|For SCD2 sources, retain quarantine evidence only for the authoritative active version and suppress superseded history.|
|Preserve schema failures|Store {{_rescued_data}} separately and create a {{RESCUED_DATA_PRESENT}} failure even when ordinary data rules pass.|


Immutable status-event sources use composite business identities in quarantine because {{status_event_id}} alone can collide:

||Event source||Quarantine identity||
|{{account_transaction_status_event}}|{{status_event_id}} + {{account_txn_id}}|
|{{atm_transaction_status_event}}|{{status_event_id}} + {{account_txn_id}}|
|{{payment_gateway_status_event}}|{{status_event_id}} + {{gateway_txn_id}} + {{event_parent_ref}}|
|{{card_transaction_status_event}}|{{status_event_id}} + {{card_txn_id}}|


h3. Central quarantine record


||Column||Purpose||
|{{quarantine_key}}|Deterministic SHA-256 identifier derived from the source identity, record fingerprint, and failure name.|
|{{pipeline_run_id}}|Job run that produced or later claimed the quarantine record.|
|{{source_table_name}}|Bronze source table that supplied the failed record.|
|{{source_business_key}}|Source business key or composite event identity represented as text.|
|{{bronze_record_ref}}|Human-readable reference to the original Bronze record.|
|{{failed_rule_name}}|Static rule, generated duplicate rule, or {{RESCUED_DATA_PRESENT}}.|
|{{quarantine_reason}}|{{VALIDATION_RULE_FAILURE}} or {{RESCUED_DATA_PRESENT}}.|
|{{rescued_data_json}}|Schema-rescue content; null for ordinary rule failures.|
|{{quarantine_data_payload}}|Complete rejected Bronze record captured before normalization.|
|{{quarantined_at}}|Timestamp when the quarantine record was created.|
